%%%
# A 1000-step vector autoregression with an exogenous input

Step k is $x_k \sim \mathrm{MvNormal}(\phi x_{k-1} + a u_k \mathbf{1}, \Sigma)$
with $x_0 = (0.5, 0.5, 0.5)$, a `kscan` over the input sequence $u$. The
initial state carries no density, so the trajectory has 1000 terms. The
observed path is a fixed deterministic curve.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

t = linspace(0.0, 20.0, 1000)
u = linspace(-1.0, 1.0, 1000)
point(s) = [sin(s), cos(s), sin(2.0 * s)]
traj = point.(t)
Sigma = rowstack([[1.0, 0.3, 0.0], [0.3, 1.0, 0.3], [0.0, 0.3, 1.0]])
step(prev, ui, phi, a) = MvNormal(phi .* prev .+ a * ui, Sigma)
